"harmonics.allharmonics.help"       = "An overview of all harmonic positions, sorted in zodiacal order. Each position is calculated by multiplying the ecliptic longitude of a factor by the harmonic number, modulo 360°.\n\nOn the left you see the glyph of the factor, followed by its harmonic position in degrees, minutes and seconds, and the sign it falls in.\n\nEnter a harmonic number in the field at the top. The value must be greater than 1 and at most 100,000. Both whole numbers and decimals are accepted.";
"harmonics.matches.help"            = "Here you see the harmonic matches: pairs where a radix position and a harmonic position are conjunct within the configured orb.\n\nThe left column shows the radix factor, the second column the harmonic factor that is conjunct with it. The orb shows how far apart the two positions are, and the exactness expresses how close the match is as a percentage.\n\nThe matches are sorted from most exact to least exact.";
"harmonics.drawing.help"            = "This screen shows a chart drawing with the harmonic positions of all active factors.\n\nThe wheel is always drawn with 0° Aries on the left, regardless of the ascendant. Aspects and house cusps are not shown.\n\nUse the colour icon to switch between colour and black-and-white rendering. Use the Export button to save the drawing as a PNG or PDF file.";
